7,278.058L164.562,280.479L165.377,283.013L166.181,285.678L166.965,288.457L167.731,291.348L168.478,294.349L169.213,297.485L169.935,300.758L170.639,304.138L171.33,307.653L172.009,311.305" stroke="black" stroke-width="2px" fill="none" stroke-dasharray="none"></path></g></svg><div role="region" aria-label="Long description for graph of a curve" class="sr-only"><ul><li>Moving from left to right, the curve passes from quadrant 3 to quadrant 4.</li><li>As x decreases, the curve approaches line y equals negative 7.</li><li>The curve passes through the following approximate points:<br/><ul><li>(negative 1 comma negative 7.3)</li><li>(0 comma negative 7.9)</li></ul></li></ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The graph of&nbsp;<math alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is shown, where <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a b Superscript x Baseline plus c"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>, and <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>, and <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> are constants. For how many values of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> does <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"43fd4dbd-983d-472e-9774-4bdddc6ff1f9","content":"<p>Three</p>"},{"id":"273fb577-38bb-47fe-a87e-9a3a863f8073","content":"<p>Two</p>"},{"id":"4bc462fb-1998-4288-975e-57447a847ed7","content":"<p>One</p>"},{"id":"d75d4f24-ef03-484e-87ec-b7688a06d2c5","content":"<p>Zero</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d75d4f24-ef03-484e-87ec-b7688a06d2c5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. Each point <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> on the graph of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane gives a value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> and its corresponding value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>. For any value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> for which <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, there is a corresponding point on the graph of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> with a <em>y</em>-coordinate of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0"><mn>0</mn></math>. A point with a <em>y</em>-coordinate of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0"><mn>0</mn></math> is a point where the graph intersects the <em>x</em>-axis. It's given that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a b Superscript x Baseline plus c"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> are constants. In the <em>xy</em>-plane, the graph of an equation of this form will lie entirely either above or below the horizontal line defined by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals c"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math>. The part of the graph of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> shown lies entirely below the horizontal line defined by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals negative 7"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></math>, and thus the entire graph of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> must lie below the line defined by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals negative 7"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. It follows that the graph of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> will never intersect the <em>x</em>-axis. Therefore, there are zero values of <em>x</em> for which <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"df71424b","external_id":"92038ced-e8e7-4472-a025-2fd98e61dd44","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"582b2734-0360-4c49-93c0-88df53b816f6","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg version=\"1.0.0\" width=\"370px\" height=\"336.328125px\" viewBox=\"0 0 370 336.328125\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"Graph of a curve in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 10 to 10. The y axis ranges from negative 10 to 5. Refer to long description.\"><defs><marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 -3 10 6\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" markerWidth=\"10px\" markerHeight=\"6px\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,-3 L10,0 L0,3\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></marker></defs><g class=\"graph-group\" transform=\"translate(25, 25)\"><g class=\"grid-group\"><g class=\"x-grid\"><line x1=\"156.1640625\" y1=\"311.328125\" x2=\"156.1640625\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"0\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"141.24625651041666\" y1=\"311.328125\" x2=\"141.24625651041666\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"1px\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"126.32845052083333\" y1=\"311.328125\" x2=\"126.32845052083333\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"1px\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"111.41064453124999\" y1=\"311.328125\" x2=\"111.41064453124999\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"1px\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"96.49283854166666\" y1=\"311.328125\" x2=\"96.49283854166666\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576