span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e312081b/img_010_a3924944.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x plus 5, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, 2 x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":11,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959621,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"e312081b","skill_cd":"P.A.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","createDate":1691007959621,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"027123-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"09d3d2eb-5974-4e59-a9f5-68c66d0659d8","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"027123-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"\"></span> </span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following is equivalent to the given expression?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x minus 2\"></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x plus 2\"></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x minus 8\"></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x plus 8\"></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. Using the associative and commutative properties of addition, the given expression <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x plus 5, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, 2 x minus 3, close parenthesis \"></span> can be rewritten as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x plus 2 x, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, 5 minus 3, close parenthesis\"></span>. Adding these like terms results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x plus 2\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from adding <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x minus 5, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, 2 x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span>. Choice C is incorrect and may result from adding <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x minus 5, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, 2 x minus 3, close parenthesis\"></span>. Choice D is incorrect and may result from adding <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x plus 5, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, 2 x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959621,"updateDate":1691007959621}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959621, 1691007959621),
    ($SATQ$e51bf5b1$SATQ$, $SATQ$6291292e-680f-4ffb-9f2e-4bf638eaee8d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Equivalent expressions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following expressions has a factor of <math alttext="x plus 2 b"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is a positive integer constant?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"5e4efbc9-6073-492b-bfd5-e7907751498e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 7 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"19c6e451-01fd-4c87-b850-7f75fef8c92c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 28 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>28</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b2bb0ea3-5006-4d9b-a72e-e0a2dcaed880","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 42 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>42</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3ff6d499-ae66-4061-8229-c177ae90ce3d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 49 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>49</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["3ff6d499-ae66-4061-8229-c177ae90ce3d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. Since each choice has a term of <math alttext="3 x squared"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which can be written as <math alttext="left parenthesis 3 x right parenthesis left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, and each choice has a term of <math alttext="14 b"><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, which can be written as <math alttext="left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 b right parenthesis"><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, the expression that has a factor of <math alttext="x plus 2 b"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is a positive integer constant, can be represented as <math alttext="left parenthesis 3 x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 2 b right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Using the distributive property of multiplication, this expression is equivalent to <math alttext="3 x left parenthesis x plus 2 b right parenthesis plus 7 left parenthesis x plus 2 b right parenthesis"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="3 x squared plus 6 x b plus 7 x plus 14 b"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>. Combining the <em>x</em>-terms in this expression yields <math alttext="3 x squared plus left parenthesis 7 plus 6 b right parenthesis x plus 14 b"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>. It follows that the coefficient of the&nbsp;<em>x</em>-term is equal to&nbsp;<math alttext="7 plus 6 b"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math>. Thus, from the given choices,&nbsp;<math alttext="7 plus 6 b"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math> must be equal to <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="28"><mn>28</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="42"><mn>42</mn>
</math>, or <math alttext="49"><mn>49</mn>
</math>. Therefore,&nbsp;<math alttext="6 b"><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math> must be equal to <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math>, or <math alttext="42"><mn>42</mn>
</math>, respectively, and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> must be equal to&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 0 Over 6 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>0</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 21 Over 6 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 35 Over 6 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 42 Over 6 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>42</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, respectively. Of these four values of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>, only <math alttext="StartFraction 42 Over 6 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>42</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math>, is a positive integer. It follows that <math alttext="7 plus 6 b"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math> must be equal to <math alttext="49"><mn>49</mn>
</math> because this is the only choice for which the value of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is a positive integer constant. Therefore, the expression that has a factor of <math alttext="x plus 2 b"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext="3 x squared plus 49 x plus 14 b"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>49</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. If this expression&nbsp;has a factor of&nbsp;<math alttext="x plus 2 b"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, then the value of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math>, which isn't positive.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. If this expression has a factor of <math alttext="x plus 2 b"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, then the value of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="StartFraction 21 Over 6 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, which isn't an integer.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. If this expression&nbsp;has a factor of <math alttext="x plus 2 b"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, then the value of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="StartFraction 35 Over 6 EndFraction"><mfrac>
<mn>35</mn>
<mn>6</mn>
</mfrac>
</math>, which isn't an integer.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e51bf5b1","external_id":"6291292e-680f-4ffb-9f2e-4bf638eaee8d","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"55fb52d9-d59c-4696-97b5-b3ba796efa8d","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.A.","skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following expressions has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is a positive integer constant?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"5e4efbc9-6073-492b-bfd5-e7907751498e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 7 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"19c6e451-01fd-4c87-b850-7f75fef8c92c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 28 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>28</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b2bb0ea3-5006-4d9b-a72e-e0a2dcaed880","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 42 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>42</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3ff6d499-ae66-4061-8229-c177ae90ce3d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 49 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>49</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["3ff6d499-ae66-4061-8229-c177ae90ce3d"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. Since each choice has a term of <math alttext=\"3 x squared\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which can be written as <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 3 x right parenthesis left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, and each choice has a term of <math alttext=\"14 b\"><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, which can be written as <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 b right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, the expression that has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is a positive integer constant, can be represented as <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 3 x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 2 b right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Using the distributive property of multiplication, this expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"3 x left parenthesis x plus 2 b right parenthesis plus 7 left parenthesis x plus 2 b right parenthesis\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 6 x b plus 7 x plus 14 b\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>. Combining the <em>x</em>-terms in this expression yields <math alttext=\"3 x squared plus left parenthesis 7 plus 6 b right parenthesis x plus 14 b\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>. It follows that the coefficient of the&nbsp;<em>x</em>-term is equal to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"7 plus 6 b\"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math>. Thus, from the given choices,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"7 plus 6 b\"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math> must be equal to <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math>, or <math alttext=\"49\"><mn>49</mn>\n</math>. Therefore,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"6 b\"><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math> must be equal to <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math>, or <math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math>, respectively, and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> must be equal to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 0 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>0</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 21 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 35 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 42 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>42</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, respectively. Of these four values of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, only <math alttext=\"StartFraction 42 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>42</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math>, is a positive integer. It follows that <math alttext=\"7 plus 6 b\"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math> must be equal to <math alttext=\"49\"><mn>49</mn>\n</math> because this is the only choice for which the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is a positive integer constant. Therefore, the expression that has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 49 x plus 14 b\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>49</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. If this expression&nbsp;has a factor of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, then the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, which isn't positive.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. If this expression has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, then the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 21 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, which isn't an integer.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. If this expression&nbsp;has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, then the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 35 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>35</mn>\n<mn>6</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>, which isn't an integer.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554983,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"e51bf5b1","skill_cd":"P.A.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","createDate":1743430554983,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"6291292e-680f-4ffb-9f2e-4bf638eaee8d","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"55fb52d9-d59c-4696-97b5-b3ba796efa8d","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following expressions has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is a positive integer constant?</p>","keys":["3ff6d499-ae66-4061-8229-c177ae90ce3d"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"5e4efbc9-6073-492b-bfd5-e7907751498e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 7 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"19c6e451-01fd-4c87-b850-7f75fef8c92c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 28 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>28</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b2bb0ea3-5006-4d9b-a72e-e0a2dcaed880","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 42 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>42</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3ff6d499-ae66-4061-8229-c177ae90ce3d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 49 x plus 14 b\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>49</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. Since each choice has a term of <math alttext=\"3 x squared\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which can be written as <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 3 x right parenthesis left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, and each choice has a term of <math alttext=\"14 b\"><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, which can be written as <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 b right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, the expression that has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is a positive integer constant, can be represented as <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 3 x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 2 b right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Using the distributive property of multiplication, this expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"3 x left parenthesis x plus 2 b right parenthesis plus 7 left parenthesis x plus 2 b right parenthesis\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 6 x b plus 7 x plus 14 b\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>. Combining the <em>x</em>-terms in this expression yields <math alttext=\"3 x squared plus left parenthesis 7 plus 6 b right parenthesis x plus 14 b\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>. It follows that the coefficient of the&nbsp;<em>x</em>-term is equal to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"7 plus 6 b\"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math>. Thus, from the given choices,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"7 plus 6 b\"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math> must be equal to <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math>, or <math alttext=\"49\"><mn>49</mn>\n</math>. Therefore,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"6 b\"><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math> must be equal to <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math>, or <math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math>, respectively, and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> must be equal to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 0 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>0</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 21 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 35 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 42 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>42</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, respectively. Of these four values of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, only <math alttext=\"StartFraction 42 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>42</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math>, is a positive integer. It follows that <math alttext=\"7 plus 6 b\"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi></math> must be equal to <math alttext=\"49\"><mn>49</mn>\n</math> because this is the only choice for which the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is a positive integer constant. Therefore, the expression that has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 49 x plus 14 b\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>49</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>b</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. If this expression&nbsp;has a factor of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, then the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, which isn't positive.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. If this expression has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, then the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 21 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, which isn't an integer.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. If this expression&nbsp;has a factor of <math alttext=\"x plus 2 b\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, then the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 35 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>35</mn>\n<mn>6</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>, which isn't an integer.</p>","externalid":"6291292e-680f-4ffb-9f2e-4bf638eaee8d","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1743430554983,"updateDate":1743430554983}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554983, 1743430554983),
    ($SATQ$e53add44$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$029350-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference " xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1"><p class="standalone_statement style:1 "><span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53add44/img_000_97bc49e5.png" alt="S of n, equals, 38,000 times a, to the n power"></span></span></p></div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The function <span class="italic">S</span> above models the annual salary, in dollars, of an employee <span class="italic">n</span> years after starting a job, where <span class="italic">a</span> is a constant. If the employee&rsquo;s salary increases by 4% each year, what is the value of <span class="italic">a </span>?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">0.04</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">0.4</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1.04</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1.4</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. A model for a quantity <span class="italic">S</span> that increases by a certain percentage per time period <span class="italic">n</span> is an exponential function in the form <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53add44/img_001_3e6a3504.png" alt="S of n equals, I times, open parenthesis, 1 plus r over 100, close parenthesis, to the n power"></span>, where <span class="italic">I</span> is the initial value at time <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53add44/img_002_20e2de42.png" alt="n equals 0 "></span> for <span class="italic">r</span>% annual increase. It&rsquo;s given that the annual increase in an employee&rsquo;s salary is 4%, so <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53add44/img_003_b858fce4.png" alt="r equals 4"></span>. The initial value can be found by substituting 0 for <span class="italic">n</span> in the given function, which yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53add44/img_004_2f8f4f96.png" alt="S of 0 equals 38,000"></span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53add44/img_005_5e95d7c8.png" alt="I equals 38,000"></span>. Substituting these values for <span class="italic">r</span> and <span class="italic">I</span> into the form of the exponential function <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53add44/img_006_3e6a3504.png" alt="S of n equals, I times, open parenthesis, 1 plus r over 100, close parenthesis, to the n power"></span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53add44/img_007_67228959.png" alt="S of n equals, 38,000 times, open parenthesis, 1 plus 4 over 100, close parenthesis, to the n power"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53add44/img_008_3b12eabb.png" alt="S of n equals, 38,000 times, 1 point 0 4 to the n power"></span>. Therefore, the value of <span class="italic">a</span> in the given function is 1.04.<p>Choices A, B, and D are incorrect and may result from incorrectly representing the annual increase in the exponential function.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
